#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:706
msgid "Scrapers and bots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:708
msgid "Block (403) the User-Agents in the list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:709
msgid "Block requests without a User-Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:710
msgid "Block fake Googlebot, Bingbot, Applebot and Yandex"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:710
msgid "The IP is checked against the official Google and Bing lists and with reverse DNS. Real search engines always pass, without limits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:711
msgid "Browsers only: 403 for pages without Accept-Language or without “Mozilla/” in the User-Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:711
msgid "Stops most scripts. Link previews (Facebook, Viber, WhatsApp etc.) in the “Always allowed” list pass."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:712
msgid "Block headless and fake browsers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:712
msgid "Blocks Chrome running without a window when it says so in its headers (“HeadlessChrome”), and, on HTTPS, scripts that copy the User-Agent of Chrome, Edge or Firefox without the Sec-Fetch headers every modern browser sends. It catches common tools and cheap scrapers, not every automated browser: one that is carefully disguised (e.g. Puppeteer with “stealth”, or Selenium with a visible Chrome) sends the same headers as a person. The page limits, the human check and the bot trap still apply to those. In-app browsers (Android WebView) are not checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:713
#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:163
#: includes/class-pncp-status.php:248
msgid "Bot trap"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:713
msgid "Invisible link on every page, disallowed in robots.txt. Whoever opens it is blocked temporarily, even if it pretends to be a browser. Visitors do not see it, and another site cannot trap them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:714
msgid "User-Agents to block (one per line, matches anywhere in the User-Agent, case-insensitive):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:714
msgid "It contains two AI categories: training crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot, Google-Extended etc.) and AI search / assistants (OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot etc.). You can allow the second one in the next section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:717
msgid "AI search and training"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:719
msgid "Allow AI search engines and assistants (not training crawlers)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:719
#, php-format
msgid "So the site appears in AI search answers with a link, without being given for model training. Allowed: %s. They are also removed from the robots.txt Disallow and from the server rules. The page limit still applies, because the User-Agent can be spoofed."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:720
msgid "Verify AI search bots with their official IP lists (OpenAI, Perplexity, Anthropic)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:720
msgid "With AI search allowed: the real OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Claude-SearchBot and Claude-User are never limited or blocked, and requests that only use their name get a 403 (“Fake AI search bot”). The lists are downloaded once a day; until then nothing changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:721
msgid "Declare AI crawlers in robots.txt (Disallow)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:721
msgid "Applies to the virtual robots.txt of WordPress. If a physical robots.txt file exists, it takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:722
msgid "Content Signals in robots.txt: search yes, AI training no"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:722
msgid "A line that says what the content may be used for (contentsignals.org): search=yes, ai-train=no, and ai-input according to “Allow AI search engines”. It does not block anything; it is a statement of your terms that well-behaved companies read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:727
msgid "Always allowed User-Agents (link previews, price comparison platforms, monitoring):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:727
msgid "They override the bot list and “Browsers only”. The page limit applies to them too, because the User-Agent is easy to spoof. To accept an entry only from specific IPs, add @ and the addresses, e.g. Skroutz@203.0.113.0/24."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:728
msgid "Always allowed IPs / CIDR (office, ERP, monitoring), one per line:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:728
msgid "They are never checked, never count towards limits and are never blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:733
msgid "IPs / CIDR that are always blocked (403), one per line:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:733
msgid "For example a scraper's server or a hosting network you see in the log. The “Always allowed IPs” take precedence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:734
msgid "Referrer domains that are always blocked (403), one per line, e.g. copy-site.example:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:734
msgid "Requests that come from links or embeds on these sites. Each entry also covers its subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:735
msgid "Hide usernames from visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:735
msgid "?author=1, 2, 3… returns “page not found” instead of the redirect to /author/username/, the REST API does not list users, and the users sitemap is removed. Logged-in users see everything as before. Author archives with a link stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:738
msgid "Limits per IP"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:740
msgid "Pages per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:740
msgid "Starting value: 60. Above the limit it returns 429. Be careful with networks that share an IP (companies, mobile carriers) and with CDNs: set the “Real visitor IP” correctly first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:741
msgid "Searches (?s=) per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:741
msgid "Search is heavy for the server and a favourite of scrapers. Starting value: 20."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:742
msgid "REST API (/wp-json/) and GraphQL requests per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:742
msgid "Only read requests from visitors. Cart, checkout and forms (POST) do not count. Starting value: 60."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:743
msgid "“Page not found” (404) per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:743
msgid "Scrapers guess addresses (?p=1, 2, 3…, old product URLs) to find content. Missing images, CSS, scripts and the favicon do not count. Starting value: 30."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:744
msgid "Sitemaps per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:744
msgid "Scrapers read the sitemap first to find every page. Covers the sitemaps of WordPress, Rank Math, Yoast and similar plugins. Google, Bing and the other verified search engines are never limited. Starting value: 5."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:749
msgid "Stricter page limit for visitors who have not shown they are people"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:749
msgid "A small script waits for the visitor's first real interaction (scroll, tap, key or mouse movement), solves a light challenge in the background and receives a cookie for 7 days. Nobody sees a captcha or a window. Visitors without the cookie (scripts, and people with JavaScript turned off) get the limit below instead of the normal page limit. Search engines and verified AI search bots are not affected. It works with page caches such as WP Rocket. A determined scraper can repeat the steps, but each of its IPs has to do the work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:750
msgid "Pages per minute without the cookie (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:750
msgid "Starting value: 20. A person reads far fewer pages per minute, and gets the cookie with the first scroll or tap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:755
msgid "Download the free country database (DB-IP Lite, once a month)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:755
msgid "Needed when the site is not behind Cloudflare or Bunny CDN. About 5 MB to download, stored as two small files in uploads/scrapelock-geo. Behind Cloudflare the country that Cloudflare sends is used, behind Bunny the one Bunny sends (when it reaches the site directly from Bunny), and the database is not needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:756
msgid "Blocked countries (403), two-letter codes separated by commas, e.g. CN, RU:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:756
msgid "Search engines, verified AI search bots and the “Always allowed” list are never blocked by country. People who travel or use a VPN appear with the country of their connection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:757
msgid "Countries with a stricter page limit, e.g. those your customers do not come from:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:758
msgid "Pages per minute for these countries (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:758
msgid "Starting value: 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:766
msgid "Block after this many violations within 10 minutes (0 = never):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:766
msgid "Violation: every minute in which the IP exceeded a limit, and every fake Googlebot. The trap blocks immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:767
msgid "Block duration (minutes):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:768
msgid "Early check: block known bots before the theme and the other plugins load"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:768
msgid "Adds the small file wp-content/mu-plugins/scrapelock-early.php, which stops blocked IPs and referrers, temporarily blocked IPs and User-Agents in the bot list with less server load. Search engines, logged-in users, forms and feeds are left to the normal check. It is removed when you turn this off or deactivate the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:770
msgid "The file could not be created (the server does not allow direct file writes to wp-content/mu-plugins). The normal check works as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:773
msgid "Pre-cache check: apply the page limit and blocks also to pages served from the page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:773
msgid "Page caches such as WP Rocket serve stored pages before any plugin loads, so a bot that looks like a browser could read them without a limit. This adds one line at the top of wp-config.php that loads a small check before the cache: always-blocked IPs, temporarily blocked IPs and the “Pages per minute” limit. Counters are kept in APCu or in wp-content/scrapelock-precheck. Search engines, logged-in users, forms, wp-admin and the REST API are left to the normal check. The line and the files are removed when you turn this off or deactivate the plugin."
